cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Divinity in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Divinity: automatic timeseries forecasting with honest prediction intervals"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: drds1
    email: drds.gh1@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/drds1/divinity"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/divinity-forecast/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
keywords:
  - forecasting
  - time series
  - ARIMA
  - seasonality
  - prediction intervals
abstract: >-
  Divinity is a Python library for automatic univariate timeseries
  forecasting. It fits regression with ARIMA errors, chooses the trend,
  Fourier seasonal terms, evolving seasonality and ARIMA order itself, and
  returns forecasts with calibrated prediction intervals.
